Licenses for dickinsonre/swmm-second-brain

Chosen by Robert Dickinson on 16 November 2026. The repository has two licenses,
by part, and some files under raw/ that are not his keep their own terms.

1. Code: the MIT License (full text below)
   tools/

2. Text and data: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
   wiki/, index.md, log.md, README.md, CLAUDE.md, ONTOLOGY.md, ontology/,
   and Robert Dickinson's own writing in raw/: raw/linkedin/, raw/swmm5org/,
   raw/apps/, raw/notes/ and raw/swmm-brain/.
   You may copy, adapt and share it for any purpose if you credit
   "Robert Dickinson, swmm-second-brain, https://github.com/dickinsonre/swmm-second-brain",
   link to the license and say what you changed.
   License: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
   Legal code: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

3. Files that keep their own terms
   raw/manuals/       Reports of U.S. government agencies (EPA, USGS, FHWA), in the
                      public domain in the United States. The SWMM 4.4 block
                      documentation in raw/manuals/swmm44/ keeps the terms of its
                      2004 CDM/OSU distribution. See raw/manuals/_SOURCE.md.
   raw/openswmm/      Thread titles and names as openswmm.org shows them. The titles
                      and the posts behind them belong to their writers; the counts
                      are CC BY 4.0 as above.
   raw/ports/         Each README carries the license of its own repository.
   raw/papers/        Journal papers by other authors, each under its own license.
                      Kukkonen et al. (2022), Automation in Construction 134,
                      104067, is open access under CC BY 4.0, (c) 2021 The
                      Authors. See raw/papers/_SOURCE.md.
   Quotations of other people's work inside any file remain theirs.

AI use: Claude (Anthropic) wrote the tools and the wiki pages at Robert Dickinson's
direction; README.md says what it did. AI is not an author of any part.

